{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLkPuokVdTGfvErFNit9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #276 to the engineer with status `done`, and wrote the result to `.ard/276/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **Plan roles:** only `triage:engineer`. It's the only triage role in this repository besides lead, so there's no architect, product-manager or documentation-planner to add.\n- **Worker:** `engineer`.\n- **Reviewers:** `eng-review` has no `when:` rule in the config, so it runs on the PR anyway and I didn't add any `review:` entries.\n\nThe issue is a concrete, owner-decided change. It adds a per-role `network` setting that defaults to on. It also adds the advisory warnings, enforces `--network none` for the worker's test step under Docker, and updates the starter prompts in `internal/roles/` and the proposal text. The files it names (`docker.go`, `env.go`, `hostwarn.go`, `prompt.go`, `internal/roles/`) all exist. It doesn't ask agents to change `.ard/` or `.github/`, and it leaves the live `.ard/` prompt copies to a separate human PR.\n\nThe file's open issues tell maintainers:\n- **No architect role:** the engineer plan and eng-review carry the design weight for a change that spans several packages and touches the security docs.\n- **Protected path:** the chart's NetworkPolicy comment is under `deploy/`, so the PR will wait for human approval.\n- **Policy change:** the new prompt text changes how future triage leads route work that needs network-only inputs, so a maintainer should treat it as a policy decision."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":821,"cache_read_input_tokens":13693,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":821},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"con